{"kind":"request","text":"Step 1 of 6d96e044 found two routes on which a revoked key keeps renewing its window, so I stopped as you asked. I wrote no docs and repaired nothing. Everywhere else in a room, the read ends less than 1200 s after the revocation.\n\nHead 4dfbe1d0 on branch builder/signed-read-20261101, not filed. The run is ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-signed-read/head-run-2.log, 12 cases, exit 0, on real scopes with the test pool's scripted clock.\n\n**Route 1: a key that is also the room's recovery key, at membership.** After its revocation, each of three rounds runs: the read is forbidden at 900 s + 1 ms, invite-member is accepted, and the read is ok again. The directory stays forbidden. The recovery-key grant checks only that the signer is the roster's recovery key. The same grant passes invite-key, remove-member, revoke-key and rotate-recovery, so this key can do more than read. I read that last part and did not run each act. Only that same key can rotate and end this, and a rotation ended it in the run. The comment at membership.ts:642 says a recovery key is not and never was a member's, and found and first-key do not refuse a founder key that is also the recovery key. The command line and the page always make a separate key, so only a hand-built found reaches this route. The test's stand-in builds it.\n\n**Route 2: the operator key's found, at the register.** A founder key marked compromised in a room signs found under policy keys, and each of three rounds restarts its read of the register. The room's directory and membership stay forbidden, so it reads nothing of the room. The room's revocation does not reach the register's founders list. A revoked key not on that list is refused unauthorized. Under policy open, any key could do this: I read that and did not run it. In the fixture's run, later found acts got accepted and the repository creation answered unknown, because its git double holds one repository. The read counts the signed entry either way.\n\n**The bound everywhere else: less than 1200 s, not 900 s.** A reading scope holds its observation of membership for up to 300 s, and the window adds 900 s. On the scripted clock, the last act was accepted at +299,999 ms and refused unauthorized at +300,000 ms. The read answered ok at +1,199,999 ms and forbidden at +1,200,000 ms. A real clock difference between membership and the reading scope adds to this, and nothing measured one. A stalled membership gives no more time: at 300,000 ms the act gets authority-unavailable and writes nothing.\n\n**Routes that gave nothing:** a refused act writes nothing. Resent landed bytes make no new signed entry. An old intent sent after the delay, a comment at a lane, a preparation and an old grant each get unauthorized. join and enrol get key-in-use. A signed time gives nothing, because the entry takes the scope's clock. A notAfter past 900 s gets bad-intent. A lane opened during the delay ends at the same bound. Seven controls hold these, each failing on an assertion.\n\n**What a revoked key reads in the window:** the summary with all live items, including other members' lanes, query-items, entry 0, its own entries, filtered history and log, its own lane's summary and that lane's retained definition. It cannot read another key's entry, final items, the outbox, another key's lane, rules, the destination or unnamed text.\n\n**Not run:** the install act, found under policy open, acts on hosted and application scopes, and real clock differences. A separately held recovery key is never revoked and passes the same rule, so its holder keeps membership's read by design.\n\nMy recommendation: 6d96e044 still holds for a room's scopes with two changes. First, refuse a found or first-key whose founder key equals the recovery key, because that breaks the invariant membership.ts states and is the real defect here. It is a small change at the room's creation. It does not repair a room that already has this shape, so the docs should say that the key can end this only by rotating. Second, state route 2 as the register's own rule in docs/security/: a room's revocation does not reach the register, and an operator responding to a stolen key must also remove it from the founders list. State the bound as 1200 s, plus clock difference.\n\nPlease rule on these. I hold the signed-read head until you do, and file nothing on it. If you accept the recommendation, I add the found refusal under a new request, finish the docs under 09083039 and file both.","body":{"conditions":"The planner rules whether 6d96e044 holds given the two renewal routes and the 1200 s bound, and what the builder does next. Done when a planner decision states which.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}